## 🧠 Part 2 — Architecture & Design Evaluation

### ✅ Strengths
- **Defense-in-Depth**: VPN + auth + firewall + anomaly detection → layered security
- **Self-Healing Loop**: Monitor → Detect → Auto-Restart → Alert → Update → Backup
- **Dependency Caching**: Docker copies deps first → fast, efficient rebuilds
- **Reproducible**: Everything in Compose + versioned configs → rebuild anywhere
- **Least Privilege**: Admin only via VPN; no account passwords exposed
- **Test-Driven**: Every component has clear AAA-pattern test cases

### ⚠️ Gaps to Address
| Gap | Impact | Priority |
|---|---|---|
| No centralized logging | Harder to correlate across services | Medium |
| No Grafana dashboards yet | Metrics exist but lack unified view | Medium |
| No documented restore procedure | Backup configured, restore not yet scripted | **High** |
| No CI/CD pipeline | Manual deploy only — no auto-test/deploy | Medium |
| No secret management | `.env` file only — no vault/encryption-at-rest | **High** |
| No chaos-automation tests | Self-healing logic not yet validated under failure | Low |

